# Reproduction for STM32WBA55_GPDMA: GPDMA_CxBR1.BNDT is a number of bytes, but the model
# decrements it by 1 per data beat, so 16- and 32-bit transfers copy 2 or 4 times the block.
#
# No Renode platform instantiates STM32WBA55_GPDMA, so it is added to the STM32WBA52 platform
# at the address from stm32wba52xx.h (GPDMA1_BASE_NS = 0x40020000, 8 channels, IRQ 29-36;
# cmsis-device-wba v1.10.0). No software is needed: the test programs the channel directly.

# Fixed copy of the model (class STM32WBA55_GPDMA_Fixed), loaded at run time.
include $ORIGIN/STM32WBA55_GPDMA_Fixed.cs

$name?="TestMachine"
$repl?=@platforms/cpus/stm32wba52.repl

using sysbus
mach create $name
machine LoadPlatformDescription $repl
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "gpdma1: DMA.STM32WBA55_GPDMA_Fixed @ sysbus 0x40020000 { numberOfChannels: 8; [0-7] -> nvic@[29-36] }"
